# ADV-153: request the Advanced Navigation device store a new Installation Alignment
# (ANPP packet 185, "Installation Alignment Packet") - the fixed rotation between the IMU's own
# body frame and the vehicle/reference frame it's physically mounted in.
#
# This service only ever sets a roll/pitch offset (a "make the sensor think it's level"
# correction) - yaw/heading alignment is intentionally left untouched (sent as 0 offset), since
# heading is separately handled via the dual-antenna GNSS solution (see
# docs/07-plan.md in the certus_eval repo).
#
# IMPORTANT: the vehicle must be stationary on a LEVEL surface when this is called. Any actual
# ground tilt present at calibration time will be misinterpreted as sensor mounting misalignment
# and (if `permanent` is true) baked into the device's persisted configuration until corrected
# again.
# (Certus ANPP: https://docs.advancednavigation.com/certus/ANPP/InstallationAlignmentPacket.htm)

# Change Permanency.
# If this is set to false (0) the change will happen but will not be saved to onboard flash. Upon
# restarting the device it will reset to the last permanent alignment.
# If this is set to true (1) the change will occur and will overwrite the flash memory on the
# device. This state will be saved and used when the device is restarted.
bool permanent

# Roll offset in radians (rotation about the vehicle's forward/X axis) - the fixed tilt to
# subtract out, typically the sensor's own reported roll while sitting stationary and level.
float64 roll

# Pitch offset in radians (rotation about the vehicle's left/Y axis) - the fixed tilt to subtract
# out, typically the sensor's own reported pitch while sitting stationary and level.
float64 pitch

---
# Response

# Acknowledgement response from device
adnav_interfaces/RawAcknowledge acknowledgement
